      "id": "IBO-01",
      "chapter": "normalization",
      "anchor": "normalization-initial-branching-moment",
      "title": "A translated highest vector follows the small diagonal to square-root accuracy",
      "hypotheses": "The fixed compression frame places the small diagonal d′ in the upper block of the conjugate of diag(d). Let π have admissible parameter λ+td at t≥1 with the stated opposite-sign gap.",
      "statement": "A conjugated unit lowest-type highest vector η satisfies Qₜ(η) ≤ C₀t. The order-t diagonal error cancels exactly, while squared root derivatives grow at most linearly.",
      "equations": [
        "normalization-initial-branching-energy"
      ],
